# Line endings.
#
# Everything text is stored LF in the repository and checked out in the
# platform's own ending, so a Windows working tree is CRLF and a Linux
# one is LF and neither shows the other as modified. Before this file
# existed, the two disagreed and produced a 43,704-line diff with no
# content change in it - which is the kind of thing that buries a real
# change rather than showing it.
* text=auto

# Binaries, named rather than left to content detection. Git's sniffing
# is good, but a vector font or a compiled resource that got normalised
# would be corrupted silently and the damage would be committed.
*.res binary
*.RES binary
*.ico binary
*.dcr binary
*.fnt binary
*.bmp binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.hlp binary
*.HLP binary
*.gid binary
*.GID binary
*.lib binary
*.dcu binary
*.exe binary
*.zip binary
# The legacy .CS2 fixtures are byte fixtures: the whole point of them
# is that the bytes are what a pre-port CADSys wrote. Never normalised.
*.CS2 binary
*.cs2 binary

# DXF is text, but TEST.DXF is a parser fixture: it is read byte for
# byte by the DXF tests, so it stays exactly as it was written.
*.dxf -text
*.DXF -text
